 "case": "N28-NO-TEAM-POS",
 "says": "A person on a local profile with no Team, no provider connection and no carrier binding binds this device's key and the checkout and registers one repository source for its decisions, all on this device. They select records 12 to 18 of one Claude Code session transcript, stating that its text may be processed locally, with no prompt log, for this repository only, and ask for its memory to be captured into that named source. The owner reads exactly that span (source.observe, nothing written), the packaged local adapter extracts one memory entry from those bytes (source.capture.record, at the head the source's registration committed: a draft capture and the extraction run that produced it), and the person stores a candidate choice extracted from that capture (memory.candidate.store). Every answer comes back with provider_effect not_applicable, the capture and the candidate both name the destination source the person requested, and the candidate names the capture and the exact span bytes it rests on. No step signs in, reaches a provider or a carrier, or calls any Team operation, and nothing here is committed to a destination beyond the local bindings and the registration.",
